# Project: map_tests

Procedural world-map preview. Desktop app.

## Tech stack

- **Desktop / UI**: Rust, Bevy + egui (`bevy_egui`)
- **World**: Rust (`noise`, `rayon`, `serde`)

## Architecture

- Rust is the only source of truth for terrain — UI only renders
- `session.rs` / `app.rs` call `world::grid` / settlement / ecology on a **worker thread**
- Texture compose: terrain + habitat wash + roads + settlements → Bevy `Image` (`render.rs`) shown via egui
- Three LOD levels: global → region → chunk
- Seed: `u64`. Params: `TerrainGenParams`

## Directory layout

```
src-tauri/                 # Rust app crate
  src/
    main.rs                # Bevy entry + map texture sync
    lib.rs
    session.rs             # map/sim state (no egui)
    app.rs                 # egui UI + LOD + legends
    colors.rs              # biome colors
    render.rs              # compose map RGBA / ColorImage
    settlements_draw.rs    # settlements + roads (RGBA)
    ecology_draw.rs        # habitat wash + life summaries
    world/                 # sampler, grid, biome, river, settlement, ecology, …
docs/                      # Polish notes (seed, plans, migration)
AGENTS.md
```

## Domain rules

- **Determinism**: same seed + same params → same world
- **6 shape profiles**: Radial, Ellipse, SquareBump, Irregular, Archipelago, Continents
- Profile from `seed % 6` (default seed `6` → Ellipse)
- Derived streams via `prng`, not a separate global RNG
- Run: `cargo run` in `src-tauri` (no web frontend)
